From 45839c0654d00c66fead83c0923e19e54f6202d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 21:33:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Examples run with the float numerical type

The tolerances of the Newton solvers and of the comparisons are kept for
double and given explicitly for float, from the residuals and the errors
measured in float (comments give the values):
- ex2 (ssna303): absolute tolerance ten times the floor of the residual
  (200 N), comparison to the reference forces at 1e-3 (1.8e-4 measured);
  UMFPACK only if MFEM provides it.
- ex4 (ssna303_3d_hypre): absolute tolerance ten times the floor (0.1),
  linear solver tolerance 1e-4 (FGMRES and BoomerAMG stagnate above 1e-5).
- ex6 (rve): comparison to the analytical solution at 4e-5 (3.9e-6
  measured); the reduction of the error uses the MPI type of real instead
  of MPI_DOUBLE.
- ex7 (mox2): relative tolerance 1e-4 (stagnation at 1.6e-5), comparison
  of the mean stresses at 5e-3 (7.5e-4 measured at the end of 40 steps).
- ex8 (rjh_plate, robin_test): relative tolerance 2e-4 and absolute
  tolerances ten times the floors of the heat transfer and mechanical
  problems, statistics compared at 3e-3 (3.6e-4 measured), swelling at
  1e-6, L2 error of the Robin test at 1e-2 (9.3e-4 measured).
Double: 24/24 on the CPU. Float: all the examples but ex1 and ex3, whose
sources are tests of mfem-mgis.
---
 ex2/ssna303.cxx             | 24 +++++++++++++++++++++---
 ex4/ssna303_hypre.cxx       | 20 ++++++++++++++------
 ex6/RveNonLinearElastic.cxx | 10 ++++++++--
 ex7/MixedOxideFuels.cxx     | 14 +++++++++++---
 ex8/Robin/robin_test.cxx    |  8 ++++++--
 ex8/Thermomechanical.cxx    | 26 ++++++++++++++++++--------
 ex8/headers/Debug.hxx       | 10 +++++++---
 7 files changed, 85 insertions(+), 27 deletions(-)

